course: dictionary
lesson: 2786
title: Words that clean and protect
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A disinfectant is a liquid or spray that kills germs on things we touch, like kitchen worktops, toilets and door handles. Germs are tiny living things that can make us ill, and bacteria are one kind of germ.
explain: Look at the context: «In Toronto, Marisol visits Grandma in a care home that smells of disinfectant and gravy.» A care home is a place where people are looked after, and gravy is food, so the smell of disinfectant must be a cleaning smell, the sharp smell of something that kills germs.
explain: Disinfectant can also describe things. In «disinfectant wipes», the word tells you what kind of wipes they are: wipes that kill germs. Disinfectant is poisonous to drink, so keep it away from small children.
fact: A disinfectant is a chemical liquid or spray that kills germs and bacteria.
fact: «Spray with disinfectant» means spray a surface so that germs are killed.
fact: As an adjective, disinfectant describes something used to kill germs, as in «disinfectant wipes».
fact: Disinfectant is used in kitchens, toilets and hospital floors to stop illness spreading.
fact: Disinfectant is poisonous to drink, so it must be kept away from small children.
exercise: «In Toronto, Marisol visits Grandma in a care home that smells of disinfectant and gravy.» What is disinfectant? | A sweet cake | *A cleaning liquid or spray that kills germs | A type of gravy | A sleepy grandmother
exercise: Why must disinfectant be kept away from small children? | It is the same as gravy | It is too sweet to share | *It is poisonous to drink | It is only for the garden
exercise: Find and copy the phrase that describes wipes that kill germs. | sleepy gravy | Grandma visits | *disinfectant wipes | care home
test: Which best describes disinfectant? | A kind of sleepy feeling | A type of fruit | A place where people live | *A liquid or spray that kills germs
test: In «a care home that smells of disinfectant and gravy», what do the words around disinfectant tell you? | The place is a sweet shop | *The place is clean and cares for people, and disinfectant is a cleaning smell | The place is in the sea | The place is a school for dogs
exam: Which phrase uses disinfectant as an adjective, describing wipes? | the disinfectant spray on the shelf | *disinfectant wipes | spray the disinfectant | a smell of disinfectant
